WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.928
The final lesson turns simulated
practice into a bounded development plan.

00:00:04.998 --> 00:00:10.331
Identify a real workflow you may observe,
the owner who can agree the frame, and the

00:00:10.401 --> 00:00:12.620
permissions needed for any experiment.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.765
Preserve confidentiality and
authoritative operating procedures.

00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:20.824
Translate the loop into the domain
while keeping the evidence discipline.

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:27.486
The source’s O&G examples are draft translations,
so do not infer WITSML compliance, safety

00:00:27.556 --> 00:00:31.033
approval, or real operational
performance from this course.

00:00:31.103 --> 00:00:36.202
In remote operations, a data-quality
review may be a suitable first workflow.

00:00:36.272 --> 00:00:41.541
An agent that changes drilling parameters
creates a different authority and consequence

00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:47.137
boundary. The same loop can guide investigation
without granting the same action rights.

00:00:47.207 --> 00:00:51.985
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:57.879
Write your next-loop proposal with owner,
permitted observation, smallest action, metric, and

00:00:57.949 --> 00:00:59.208
stop condition.

00:00:59.278 --> 00:01:04.910
Propose observing one approved data-review
task and testing a reviewable exception summary

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.668
with synthetic or explicitly permitted data.

00:01:07.738 --> 00:01:11.002
Retain human judgment and
authoritative procedures.

00:01:11.072 --> 00:01:15.083
Name the operational owner and
define success before acting.

00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:20.635
Treat real deployment evidence as the next
learning objective, not something this simulated

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:22.668
portfolio already established.

00:01:22.738 --> 00:01:24.871
What does domain translation change?

00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:27.949
A. It grants automatic operating permission B.

00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:32.478
Vocabulary and context, while
permissions still need verification C.

00:01:32.548 --> 00:01:34.404
It proves standards compliance.

00:01:34.474 --> 00:01:35.946
The best answer is B.

00:01:36.016 --> 00:01:39.984
A transferable method does not
imply transferable authority.
